WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.310
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.570
- [Narrator] The music is catchy,

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.940
it's upbeat, and it's
urging young Russian men

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.843
to join the infamous
Wagner mercenary group.

00:00:08.843 --> 00:00:13.200
(narrator speaking in foreign language)

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.820
- [Narrator] There are
also social media posts

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.470
and highly produced action movies

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.513
portraying fighters as heroes.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.720
Wagner has played a major role

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.363
helping Russia's depleted
forces in Ukraine,

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.030
but as its own losses mount,

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.670
the group needs more mercenaries to fight.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.400
It's spent months recruiting
from Russia's prison system

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.110
but stopped the practice in February

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.403
without giving a reason.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.790
With one source of recruitment gone,

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:40.890
security analysts say online propaganda

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:42.690
has become more important.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:45.960
So here's how Wagner uses this
content to glorify the war

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.330
and sell the idea of adventure and heroism

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:49.773
to potential recruits.

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:51.690
(gun shooting)

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:55.560
The movie "The Best in Hell"
was released last October.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.393
(dramatic music)

00:00:56.393 --> 00:01:01.020
(narrator speaking in foreign language)

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.150
- [Narrator] The dramatic
music, special effects

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.010
and professional camera work make it look

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.600
like a Hollywood action movie

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.060
but it's actually a Russian production.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:11.400
The one and a half hour
film showing a battle

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.080
between Russian mercenaries

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.730
and an unnamed enemy was produced

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:17.460
by Wagner's founder Yevgeny Prigozhin.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.940
He's a close ally of the Russian
president, Vladimir Putin.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.560
Security experts say this

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.410
and other such movies create
a heroic image of the group,

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:28.774
which Prigozhin can use to boost
his position within Russia.

00:01:28.774 --> 00:01:30.420
(upbeat music)

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.700
Also online are these music clips.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.140
The production is less polished

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:36.600
but the lyrics suggests that
being a mercenary for Wagner

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.900
is more exciting than
everyday life in Russia.

00:01:40.036 --> 00:01:44.453
(singer singing in foreign language)

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.040
- [Narrator] There are
even lyrics on screen

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.605
for viewers to sing along with.

00:01:48.605 --> 00:01:50.070
(upbeat music)

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:51.990
Another video, uses a female voice

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:55.350
and characters from Japanese
anime to appeal to young men.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:58.110
The Wall Street Journal wasn't
able to determine the origins

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:01.050
of these clips, but
The Journal established

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:01.883
that they've been posted

00:02:01.883 --> 00:02:03.720
on Wagner linked social media accounts

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.510
and pro-Kremlin online
communities since September

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.640
around the time Wagner
watchers say the group

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.485
expanded its recruitment efforts.

00:02:11.485 --> 00:02:14.880
(singer singing in foreign language)

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:15.840
- [Narrator] Analysts say these

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.520
and other similar videos on social media

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.050
make the war look like a video game

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.573
and trivialize violence
against Ukrainians.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.230
Some security experts say
Wagner has been desperate

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.940
for new recruits.

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.220
In January, the US State
Department said the group

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:31.980
had up to 50,000 mercenaries
fighting in Ukraine,

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.810
many of them prisoners

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:36.330
but a Russian prisoner
rights organization estimated

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:38.940
that about 40,000 either
deserted or surrendered

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:41.280
or were injured or killed.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.230
Recent Wagner videos give a glimpse

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:45.300
into the company's losses.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.370
Here Yevgeny Prigozhin laid flowers

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:49.523
at a graveyard in Russia's south.

00:02:49.523 --> 00:02:53.220
(Yevgeny speaking in foreign language)

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.720
- [Narrator] Another video show Prigozhin

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:58.260
in a morgue surrounded by
piles of black body bags.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.090
Prigozhin didn't respond to our request

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.790
for comment on Wagner's
recruitment efforts.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.770
The Kremlin also didn't
reply to our request

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:07.050
for comment on how the
company's recruitment efforts

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:09.661
help Russia's military action in Ukraine.

00:03:09.661 --> 00:03:10.860
(upbeat music)

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.110
It's hard to gauge the
effectiveness of movies

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:16.470
and music clips to promote
Wagner to potential recruits

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:19.260
but analysts say this type
of content normalizes the war

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:20.130
as well as the idea

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:23.190
that fighting for Russia
is just another career path

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:25.830
and it helps Moscow to
continue its recruitment effort

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.840
as concern mounts among many Russians

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.715
over the possibility of
a second mobilization.

00:03:30.715 --> 00:03:32.956
(lively music)
(guns shooting)

